{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"fddf7cdcbf79322d3932306c5aea07ccc730e780360c2ad13acf0e425e362114","packTokens":3287,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":215,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":273,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":616,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":2077,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nMap each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Import procurement PO and receiving data, map PO lines to lots and pens, and forecast lifecycle targets.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Track feed inventory, stock movements, forecasts, wastage, ration recipes, and ration costs.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Create pen-level feeding plans and log feeding activities, updating inventory and lot consumption and cost.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Record lot weight measurements and maintain weight histories.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Calculate feed-to-gain metrics and predictive sale/feeding insights, updating when feeding or weight events are recorded.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide operational dashboards, reports, filters, CSV/PDF exports, and yard-level summaries.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-7\",\n  \"text\": \"Create mock data and present the proposed solution, architecture, demo, testing, challenges, readiness, and go-to-market analysis.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"What user access model is required for operational and financial records?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use one shared access level for all users; do not distinguish permissions by role.\",\n  \"by\": \"Ahsan (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"When a pen contains multiple lots, how must a feeding plan allocate its planned quantity?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Require a quantity allocation to each lot and flag allocations that do not reconcile with the plan.\",\n  \"by\": \"Ahsan (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"How should the configured wastage ratio affect inventory decrements for an actual feeding event?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Decrement stock by the actual delivered quantity and apply wastage only to estimated consumption and forecasts.\",\n  \"by\": \"Ahsan (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"How should total lot weight be handled when a user records average weight and the number of animals weighed?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Calculate total measured weight as average weight multiplied by the number weighed; do not accept a conflicting independent total.\",\n  \"by\": \"Ahsan (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"What cost basis should the lot-level profitability analysis include?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Show feed cost per unit of weight gain using recorded feed costs only.\",\n  \"by\": \"Ahsan (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"How should users sign in, given that all users have the same access level?\",\n  \"answer\": \"No sign-in; anyone with the app link can access the shared workspace.\",\n  \"by\": \"Ahsan (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"When a pen contains multiple lots, how should an actual feeding quantity be attributed to those lots for lot-level consumption and cost metrics?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Allocate the actual quantity to lots in proportion to their planned quantities.\",\n  \"by\": \"Ahsan (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"Which ingredient cost should be used to calculate the cost of a saved feeding event when the ingredient's unit cost changes over time?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use the ingredient unit cost recorded when the feeding event is saved.\",\n  \"by\": \"Ahsan (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Provide a shared Feedlot web workspace that opens without sign-in or role selection and presents the same operational and financial controls to every user.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Let operators synchronize procurement from a mock source adapter and display returned PO and receiving fields, including PO line, vendor, cost, head count, weight, breed, age, and source.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Let users map one PO line to one or multiple lots and assign the lots to pens, displaying PO-line traceability, pen ID, capacity, and returned animal count.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Display affected duplicate, changed, or conflicting import records with returned conflict status, any existing mapping, and a review action.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Display each lot’s returned target weight and projected market or ship date, leaving the projected date empty when ADG is zero or negative.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Display lot-specific targets and gain assumptions when available, use the configured yard target when procurement supplies no target, and show the same configured yard target weight for all lots.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Let users view and enter feed inventory items, displaying name, category, available quantity, unit, unit cost, dry-matter percentage, energy value, storage location, and opening, received, consumed, and closing stock values.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"When a stock movement is refused because it would make inventory negative, display the returned refusal message and shortage, keep the movement form available for correction, and do not display a saved movement.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Let users configure a wastage ratio and display returned ingredient balance and shortage forecasts for daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, bi-annual, and annual horizons, using dated feeding-plan demand and wastage-adjusted estimated consumption; mark periods without a dated plan unavailable.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Let users create and view rations with name, type, ingredient quantities or as-fed proportions, dry-matter percentage, energy value, intended animal type or weight range, and returned calculated cost per pound.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Provide ration comparisons showing returned ration costs and associated lot performance or cost-of-gain values, and identify the lowest returned cost of gain when available.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"Where inventory or ration screens show ton-denominated prices, display the equivalent per-pound price in the configured currency and show calculation quantities in pounds.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"Let users generate a dated pen feeding plan from a selected ration, per-animal daily bunk rate, pen animal count, date, and planned feeding time, displaying planned quantity, quantity per animal, total feed cost, expected energy intake, and returned plan status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"For feeding plans in pens containing multiple lots, require a quantity allocation for every lot and flag any difference between allocation total and plan total; identify missing allocations and do not show an unsaved plan as saved, while displaying the single-lot allocation field for a one-lot pen.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"When a user saves an actual feeding event, display returned planned and delivered quantities, actual-minus-planned variance, feed cost, energy value, inventory decrement based on delivered quantity, feeding status, lot allocation, and the ingredient unit-cost snapshot recorded at save time.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"For events allocated to multiple lots, display each lot’s returned actual quantity allocated in proportion to planned quantities and the event cost returned at save; preserve each event’s saved unit-cost value for its cost, and display delivered-quantity inventory decrement separately from any wastage-adjusted estimated consumption.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"When actual feeding differs from the plan, show planned and actual quantities and variance, and provide an action to adjust a future plan using editable future quantities and the selected pen and ration.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"Let users record lot weight measurements with date, number of animals weighed, average weight, and notes; calculate total measured weight as average weight multiplied by number weighed and provide no editable total-weight field.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"Display lot weight measurement history as a time-ordered list of returned dated records, including average weight, number weighed, total measured weight, gain since the prior measurement, and notes when returned.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"When saved feeding or weight records are edited or voided, display returned revised balances and metrics while retaining the original record in record history.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"Where record details are displayed, show returned creator and last-changed identifiers and timestamps without a full audit-log view.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"Display returned lot feed-to-gain metrics for days on feed, total weight gain, average daily gain, total feed consumed, feed conversion ratio, feed cost per unit of weight gain, and projected ship date; calculate cost per gain using recorded feed costs only.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 23,\n  \"text\": \"After a feeding or weight event is saved, refresh displayed lot metrics and show returned feeding-adjustment or sale-timing suggestions when updated metrics and insights are returned.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 24,\n  \"text\": \"Provide an operational dashboard showing active lots and pens, animals per lot and pen, feed inventory status, ration usage, daily bunk rate per pen, planned versus actual feed, total feed consumed and cost, starting and current weight, total weight gain, average daily gain, feed-to-gain ratio, feed cost per unit of gain, energy consumed, and best- and worst-performing lots.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 25,\n  \"text\": \"Provide operational reports identifying the highest-feed-consuming pen, best feed-to-gain lot, highest-ADG lot, most-used ration, plan-versus-actual alignment, overfed or underfed pens, remaining inventory, and feed cost per unit of weight gain.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 26,\n  \"text\": \"Provide a dedicated Feed-to-Gain report with date-range, lot, breed, sex, and pen filters, showing selected filters and returned matching lots’ ADG, FCR, and cost of gain when filters are selected or changed.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 27,\n  \"text\": \"Allow the filtered Feed-to-Gain results and selected scope to be exported as CSV and PDF files.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 28,\n  \"text\": \"Provide a yard-level summary of aggregate total head, average ADG, average cost of gain, and total feed cost across active lots.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 29,\n  \"text\": \"Provide representative mock operational data for procurement, lots, pens, inventory, rations, feeding, and weights, and a project presentation page covering the proposed solution, architecture diagrams, demo walkthrough, coding prompts, testing and validation, challenges, production readiness, and go-to-market strategy and analysis.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 30,\n  \"text\": \"Render every page responsively in the web app for phone, tablet, and desktop browser widths, with touch-sized primary controls on narrow layouts.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}